<div class="page-head"><h1>Backups</h1></div>
<div class="alert info">Backups are created by <code>php bin/backup.php</code> (schedule it daily) and checked by <code>php bin/backup.php --verify</code>. A backup is only trusted once it is marked <em>verified</em>; do a full restore test at least quarterly (see docs/BACKUP_AND_RECOVERY.md).</div>
<div class="card"><?php if (!$rows): ?><p class="empty">No backups have been recorded. The platform is currently unprotected against data loss.</p><?php else: ?>
<div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Created (UTC)</th><th>File</th><th class="num">Size</th><th>SHA-256</th><th>Status</th><th>Verified</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<?php foreach ($rows as $b): ?><tr><td class="nowrap"><?= e($b['created_at']) ?></td><td class="small"><?= e($b['file']) ?></td><td class="num"><?= number_format((int)$b['size_bytes'] / 1024, 0) ?> KB</td><td class="small"><code><?= e(substr((string)$b['sha256'], 0, 12)) ?>…</code></td><td><?= badge($b['status'] === 'ok' ? 'succeeded' : 'failed') ?></td><td><?= $b['verified_at'] ? e($b['verified_at']) : '<span class="badge badge-warn">not verified</span>' ?></td></tr><?php endforeach; ?></tbody></table></div><?php endif; ?></div>
